[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Test Structure, Hooks, and Suite Organization in Cypress"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Writing maintainable and scalable end-to-end tests requires a solid understanding of how to structure your test files. Cypress uses Mocha's BDD syntax, providing a clean and intuitive way to organize tests using suites and hooks."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Test Suites (describe and context)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Test suites are used to group related tests together. Cypress provides the 'describe' function (and its alias 'context') for this purpose. Grouping tests logically makes your test runner output easier to read and helps maintain your codebase."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"describe('User Authentication Suite', () => {
  it('should allow a user to log in', () => {
    // Test implementation here
  });

  it('should show an error for invalid credentials', () => {
    // Test implementation here
  });
});"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Cypress Hooks: before, beforeEach, after, and afterEach"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Hooks help you manage setup and teardown tasks in your test suites. They reduce code duplication and ensure a clean state before each test runs. Cypress supports four types of hooks:"},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"before(): Runs once before all tests in the current block."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"beforeEach(): Runs before each individual test in the block."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"afterEach(): Runs after each individual test in the block."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"after(): Runs once after all tests in the current block have completed."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Practical Example Using beforeEach and before"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"A common use case for 'before' is seeding a database, while 'beforeEach' is frequently used to visit a specific URL or reset application state before every test."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"describe('Dashboard Feature', () => {
  before(() => {
    // Runs once before any tests run
    cy.log('Setting up global test data');
  });

  beforeEach(() => {
    // Runs before each test in this describe block
    cy.visit('/dashboard');
  });

  it('displays the user profile summary', () => {
    cy.get('.profile-summary').should('be.visible');
  });

  it('allows navigation to settings', () => {
    cy.get('#nav-settings').click();
    cy.url().should('include', '/settings');
  });
});"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Suite Organization"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep test files focused on a single feature or page component to prevent bloated files."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use descriptive strings in your 'describe' and 'it' blocks to clearly document expected behavior."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage nested 'describe' blocks to handle specific states, such as 'when logged out' versus 'when logged in'."}]
